 "pageLayoutIdOverlap": {
  "CORRECTION": "This block previously reported 'ZERO overlap, therefore page layouts are independently firm-authored'. That was WRONG - it joined on id alone. Joining on (mode, name) is the correct test and reverses the conclusion. Retained here so the error is not silently rewritten.",
  "joinOnIdAlone": {
   "sharedModeAndId": 0,
   "note": "True but MEANINGLESS - the id spaces are re-keyed per tenant, so an id join can never match."
  },
  "joinOnModeAndName": {
   "afLayouts": 88,
   "bbwLayouts": 93,
   "shared": 80,
   "onlyAF": 7,
   "onlyBBW": 12,
   "primaryTableMismatches": 0,
   "idDeltaBand": "BBW_id - AF_id: 58 of 80 shared layouts fall in +2626..+2677; most common deltas +2626 (14), +2638 (13), +2652 (7), +2653 (7). Full range 1010..2923.",
   "duplicateRowInBoth": "Both tenants carry the SAME duplicate (mode,name): LIST / 'ASG Contract Payment Details - Security Deposit'. A duplicate reproduced in both tenants is copied, not independently authored.",
   "conclusion": "Observed. ASG publishes ONE page-layout template set per tenant which then forks locally; BBW is the more advanced fork (93 vs 88, 12 layouts AF lacks). Page layouts are NOT independently firm-authored. Zero primaryTable mismatches across all 80 shared layouts means the fork diverges in inventory and ids, not in what each layout binds to.",
   "methodLesson": "Join on NAME as well as id before concluding two tenants differ. Re-keyed id blocks make an id-only join produce a false negative."
  },
